{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "patient-care",
    "title": "Patient Care",
    "order": 4
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "infection-control-hazardous-materials",
    "title": "Infection Control & Hazardous Materials",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Why Infection Control Is Non-Negotiable",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation therapy patients are frequently immunocompromised \u2014 from their cancer, from treatment, or from both. You handle multiple patients back-to-back, often touching shared equipment (couch, immobilization devices, positioning aids) between them. Consistent infection control isn't optional paperwork; it's how you avoid becoming the link that spreads infection between vulnerable patients."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Chain of Infection",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Infection spreads through a predictable chain, and breaking any single link stops transmission:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Pathogen",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 the organism itself"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Reservoir",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 where it lives and grows"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Portal of exit",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 how it leaves the reservoir"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Mode of transmission",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 direct (droplet, direct contact) or indirect (airborne, vehicle-borne/fomite, vector-borne)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Portal of entry",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 how it enters a new host"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Susceptible host",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 someone whose defenses can't fight it off"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Hand hygiene, PPE, and cleaning protocols each target a different link in this chain."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Hand Hygiene",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Hand washing is the single simplest and most effective method of environmental infection control available, and it must be performed "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "before and after every patient contact",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 no exceptions for a \"quick\" interaction."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Alcohol-based hand sanitizer is acceptable for most routine contact, but true hand washing with soap and water is required when hands are visibly soiled, and for certain organisms (like "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "C. difficile",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ") that alcohol alone won't reliably kill."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When should you perform hand hygiene relative to a patient encounter?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Before the encounter only",
              "After the encounter only",
              "Both before and after every patient"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Hand hygiene is required both before and after every single patient contact."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Asepsis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Medical asepsis",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (\"clean technique\") reduces the number of organisms present and prevents their spread \u2014 hand hygiene, cleaning surfaces, wearing gloves for routine contact."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Surgical/sterile asepsis",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (\"sterile technique\") eliminates "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "all",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " organisms from a defined field \u2014 sterile gowning and gloving, sterile draping, and maintaining a sterile field are used for invasive procedures like certain brachytherapy or line placements you may assist with."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Equipment itself requires the correct level of care: some items need only disinfection between patients, others require full sterilization."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "CDC Standard Precautions",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Standard Precautions apply to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "every patient, every time",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 regardless of known infection status, because you often don't know:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Hand hygiene"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Personal protective equipment (gloves, gowns, masks) matched to the expected exposure"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Safe handling of contaminated equipment and surfaces"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Safe disposal of linens, needles, patient supplies, and blood/body fluids"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Safe needle practices (never recap by hand)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Transmission-Based Precautions",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When a specific infection is known or suspected, Standard Precautions get layered with transmission-based precautions matched to how that organism spreads:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Contact precautions",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 gown and gloves for direct or indirect contact organisms"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Droplet precautions",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 mask for organisms spread by respiratory droplets over short distances"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Airborne precautions",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 N95 respirator and negative-pressure room for organisms that travel on tiny particles over longer distances"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient with a suspected airborne illness needs which level of respiratory protection?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Standard surgical mask",
              "N95 respirator"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Airborne precautions require an N95 (or higher) respirator, not a standard surgical mask."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Additional Precautions",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Neutropenic precautions (reverse isolation)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " protect an immunocompromised patient "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "from you and the environment",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 the direction of protection flips compared to standard precautions. Many radiation therapy patients undergoing chemotherapy fall into this category."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Be alert for signs of "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "healthcare-associated (nosocomial) infections",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 infections a patient didn't have on admission, and report anything concerning through your facility's protocol."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Handling and Disposal of Hazardous Materials",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Beyond biological infection control, you'll encounter other hazardous materials:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Chemicals",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (cleaning agents, disinfectants) \u2014 know their proper storage and handling"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Chemotherapy agents",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 require special handling precautions; patients receiving concurrent chemo may have contaminated bodily fluids for a period afterward"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Metals",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (e.g., block alloy used in shielding) \u2014 handled with appropriate precautions during fabrication/storage"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Safety Data Sheet (SDS)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " for any hazardous material tells you its risks, safe handling procedures, and what to do in case of exposure \u2014 know where your department's SDS binder or database is located."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered the chain of infection, hand hygiene, asepsis, CDC standard and transmission-based precautions, neutropenic precautions, and hazardous material handling."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The common thread across all of it: know the risk in front of you, and match your precautions to it \u2014 consistently, every patient, every time."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
